      "side": 1,
      "message": "I hadn\u0027t thought of converging the two so far, but this presents a good opportunity to brainstorm this\n\nI think `cc_library_headers` should be the rule used by most authors. `cc_api_headers` should be used only when the headers are expected to be presented to an external API domain (similar to how we have a `cc_library_headers` _and_ `cc_library_headers.llndk` _and_ `ndk_headers` in Soong today)\n\nSome brainstorming thoughts:\n1. If we make cc_api_headers a macro around cc_library_headers and make the latter private, one of the targets will always present an (unused) provider that is only meaningful to the build orchestrator, even when the headers are internal to the API domain. Also, cc_api_headers does not have any configuration transitions currently, but cc_library_headers should (can we do this in macros?)\n2. Vice versa (cc_library_headers a macro around the other), we might need to do a glob expansion in bp2build so that `hdrs` are explicitly listed in the generated BUILD files. (And probably some string parsing to map the .h files to the relevant include_dir to create the cc_api_headers targets in the macro)\n\nJin, is the idea of converging the two via a macro focussed to provide better readability/maintainalibilty of BUILD files for end users? Functionally, both approaches (macro/no_macro) should have similar effect",
      "parentUuid": "90688512_69abc4ed",
      "revId": "f24a1c50689a3c7a78bccf6e4e6d5cb3c49c2e32",
